                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "55060785",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198047108526",
                            "num_reviews": 11,
                            "playtime_forever": 83,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 83,
                            "last_played": 1568197066
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Visual and sound wise, it's all right. Nothing to write home about but quite passable. Everything else is trash. The gameplay loop consists of mindlessly running around an island collection diamonds and orbs as well as the occasional platforming puzzle. Thing is, the platforming is absolutely horrendous. It's really imprecise and you will die countless times on the most trivial jumps. And there's very little rhythmic for a \"single player platformer in first person, set in a world where everything is tied to the music\". The music's just here but doesn't really seem to affect anything. You'd think they'd have made it part of the gameplay if it's such an integral part of their pitch\nBottom line is, avoid this like the plague (not that it was on anyone's radar to begin with...)",
                        "timestamp_created": 1568198731,
